---
// Schematic drawing of three cover constructions. Not to scale, no real product.
---
<figure class="fig">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 760 260" role="img" aria-labelledby="cl-t cl-d" width="760" height="260">
    <title id="cl-t">Three Kindle cover constructions</title>
    <desc id="cl-d">Schematic drawings of a full-wrap folio with a front flap, a back cover that leaves the screen open, and a slim cover that attaches to the back of the device with magnets.</desc>
    <g font-family="sans-serif" font-size="13" fill="#1d1b18" text-anchor="middle">
      <!-- full wrap folio -->
      <g transform="translate(20,16)">
        <rect x="0" y="10" width="76" height="150" rx="6" fill="#7a5b3a"/>
        <rect x="92" y="10" width="76" height="150" rx="6" fill="#8e6c46"/>
        <rect x="76" y="10" width="16" height="150" fill="#5f4529"/>
        <rect x="104" y="24" width="52" height="108" rx="2" fill="#faf6ee" stroke="#1d1b18"/>
        <rect x="94" y="14" width="72" height="142" rx="5" fill="none" stroke="#1d1b18" stroke-dasharray="3 3" opacity=".35"/>
        <text x="84" y="188" font-weight="700">Full-wrap folio</text>
        <text x="84" y="206" fill="#4a453d">Front flap + back + spine</text>
        <text x="84" y="224" fill="#4a453d">Screen covered when closed</text>
      </g>
      <!-- back cover -->
      <g transform="translate(270,16)">
        <rect x="40" y="10" width="100" height="150" rx="12" fill="#2f5d57"/>
        <rect x="52" y="24" width="76" height="108" rx="3" fill="#faf6ee" stroke="#1d1b18"/>
        <text x="90" y="188" font-weight="700">Back cover / shell</text>
        <text x="90" y="206" fill="#4a453d">Back and edges only</text>
        <text x="90" y="224" fill="#4a453d">Screen open to the air</text>
      </g>
      <!-- magnetic attach -->
      <g transform="translate(500,16)">
        <rect x="0" y="10" width="76" height="150" rx="6" fill="#9c9078"/>
        <rect x="92" y="10" width="76" height="150" rx="6" fill="#b3a68a"/>
        <rect x="104" y="24" width="52" height="108" rx="2" fill="#faf6ee" stroke="#1d1b18"/>
        <rect x="80" y="60" width="14" height="6" rx="2" fill="#9a3b1f"/>
        <rect x="80" y="104" width="14" height="6" rx="2" fill="#9a3b1f"/>
        <text x="84" y="188" font-weight="700">Magnetic-attach folio</text>
        <text x="84" y="206" fill="#4a453d">Slim; device held by magnets</text>
        <text x="84" y="224" fill="#4a453d">Red tabs = magnet zones</text>
      </g>
    </g>
  </svg>
  <figcaption>Our own schematic, not drawn to scale and not based on any specific product. The dashed outline on the folio marks where the Kindle sits; the magnetic-attach version shows where magnets typically sit between the cover and the device back.</figcaption>
</figure>
